      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2025/08/hoka-arahi-8-review-2025.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: Full-length EVA is moderately soft with a higher 41/33 mm stack for solid impact protection, but heel landings feel clunky/medially biased while the forefoot transitions more smoothly via the rocker.",
        "Responsiveness: Energy return is low; the EVA ride is described as not responsive, with limited bounce/snappiness and a slower feel that makes faster paces harder.",
        "Stability: The H-frame, wide base, sidewalls, and moderately stiff heel counter provide mild-to-moderate guidance and lateral/medial motion control with high overall stiffness, though medial correction is less pronounced than prior J-frame versions.",
        "Durability: Durability is below average for running, with exposed EVA outsole wear showing early (around 10 miles, especially midfoot) and the midsole beginning to firm by about 40 miles."
      ]
